<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27801" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δμῳ-ή</span></b>  (<i><span class="en">
			Choerob.
			<u>in Theod.</u>
			1.405
		</span></i>) or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δμω-ή</span></b>  (both
		spellings freq. in codd.), ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαμάω</span>) prop. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>female slave taken in war,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δμῳαὶ δ᾽ ἃς Ἀχιλεὺς
			ληΐσσατο</span> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δμώς</span>)
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.28
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				9.658
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				24.643
			</span></i>: generally, <i>female slave, serving-woman,</i> only in
			pl. in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, mostly joined with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναῖκες</span>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δμῳαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					908
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1189
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. γυναῖκες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					84
				</span></i>
			; rare in Prose, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				5.1.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				1.5
			</span></i>: later in sg., <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				5.561
			</span></i>; of things, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δμωὴν . . Ἄϊδος . . μάκελλαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.1389i
				</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				i25
			</span></i>.</div>
